# Copy to .env. Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables reach the app bundle.
#
# There is ONE backend now — the FastAPI service in backend/ on port 8080. The
# Express API on 4000 is deleted. Two variables point at it because the app has
# two clients (lib/api.ts and lib/backend.ts); both default to the same place.
#
# Leave BOTH unset when running on a phone via Expo Go: the app reuses the LAN IP
# Metro is already serving from, which is the machine running the backend.

# Used by lib/api.ts. Set it when the LAN-IP guess is wrong, or on the web build:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:8080
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Used by lib/backend.ts. Same rule. Point it at the Next port instead to run
# everything through a single origin — Next proxies /v1/* to the backend
# (see apps/web/next.config.ts), so this is all you change:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://192.168.1.42:3000
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8080
